course: dictionary
lesson: 13625
title: Clear or blurred?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Indistinct describes something you cannot see, hear or remember clearly. Its opposite is distinct, which means clear and easy to tell apart. The prefix in- often means not, so indistinct means not distinct.
explain: «From inside the tent, we could hear indistinct voices through the rain.» You can tell that people are talking, but you cannot make out their words. The clue is the rain and the tent: the sound is there but it is blurred. Ask yourself what would fit: hard to hear clearly.
explain: «The shape in the fog was indistinct.» Fog makes things hard to see, so indistinct must mean blurred or faint. Test it by swapping in hard to see clearly. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Indistinct can also be an adverb, indistinctly, which tells you how someone does something. «He mumbled indistinctly into the phone.» Mumbling makes speech hard to understand, so the word shows the words were not clear.
fact: Indistinct means not clear or sharp; hard to see, hear or remember clearly.
fact: Indistinct can mean blurred or faint, as in «indistinct shapes in the fog».
fact: The adverb «indistinctly» means in a way that is not clear: «She spoke indistinctly through her scarf.»
fact: Useful phrases include an indistinct shape, indistinct voices and an indistinct memory.
fact: Indistinct is the opposite of distinct, which means clear and easy to tell apart.
exercise: «The shape in the fog was indistinct.» What does indistinct mean? | *Hard to see clearly | Very bright and shiny | Easy to read | Very large and heavy
exercise: «We heard indistinct voices behind the wall.» What does indistinct voices mean? | *Voices that are hard to make out | Voices singing a song together | Loud, cheerful voices | Voices that are very close to us
exercise: «He mumbled indistinctly into the phone.» Which word tells how he spoke? | loudly | *indistinctly | happily | clearly
exercise: «Her memory of the day was indistinct, like a dream.» What does indistinct mean here? | *Hard to remember clearly | Easy to remember word for word | Painted in bright colours | Very funny and silly
test: Which word is the opposite of indistinct? | Blurred | Faint | *Clear | Hidden
test: «The lighthouse was an indistinct shape in the mist.» What is the best meaning of indistinct? | Tall and white | Shiny and new | Loud and bright | *Blurred and hard to see
exam: Which sentence uses indistinct correctly? | The bell was so clear that we could count every chime. | *Through the fog, the lighthouse was only an indistinct shape. | Her handwriting was indistinct, so everyone could read it easily.
